a woman who not only played,

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:07.307
but we know from your experience
at the U.S. Open,

00:00:07.307 --> 00:00:09.075 align:start size:94% position:6%
will tell you what she thinks
about your playing.

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:10.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Exactly.
-And I heard that you

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:11.411 align:start size:94% position:6%
actually developed --
´Cause you didn´t

00:00:11.411 --> 00:00:13.013 align:start size:94% position:6%
have to learn
how to play tennis.

00:00:13.013 --> 00:00:14.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
You had to learn
how to play old tennis.

00:00:14.848 --> 00:00:17.283
-Like Billie Jean, exactly.
Wooden-rackets ´70s tennis.

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:20.520
Which, one time,
I was actually at a public court

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.422 size:88% position:44%
learning with a trainer,

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:24.090
and these guys were next to us,

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:27.027 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they were like,
"Oh, tight. Huh.

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:28.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
Wooden rackets.
That´s pretty cool."

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:31.464 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"I´m not being a hipster.

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:35.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´m just learning
this form of tennis for work.

00:00:35.602 --> 00:00:37.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
But all right."

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:39.339
I mean, I guess people do play
wooden-racket tennis probably.

00:00:39.339 --> 00:00:41.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, oh, I´m sure
there´s plenty of dickheads

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:42.675
in New York that are like,

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:45.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I´m gonna play with my old
Jimmy Connors racket."

00:00:45.011 --> 00:00:47.013 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It´s hard.
-I would imagine it´s hard.

00:00:47.013 --> 00:00:48.948 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you´re starting
from a place where you --

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:50.517 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean,
maybe it was easier for you

00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:52.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
because you didn´t have to
unlearn modern tennis.

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:54.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, exactly.
And it was kind of fun.

00:00:54.921 --> 00:00:57.057
Because at the end of my
lessons, once I got a little --

00:00:57.057 --> 00:00:58.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
Once I started understanding
a little bit more,

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:01.194
I would get to play for five
minutes with a modern-day racket

00:01:01.194 --> 00:01:03.963 align:start size:94% position:6%
and a different grip, and
I was like, "I can really hit!

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:05.632 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Whoa!"

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:08.101
But before that, it was just
my trainer was having to come up

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:09.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
